{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Triage (orphan-task pass): this task needs a DESIGN DECISION before implementation — escalating to operator rather than implementing.\n\nThe blocker is the ticket's own bar: remove *.retired only \"provably past causal stability\". Epic b306 (adept-hedge-stain) deliberately accepted PERMANENT retention as the storage tradeoff precisely because no stability proof exists: the tracker has no registry of clones, so no algorithm in the current model can prove that every clone has observed a compaction. Any horizon we pick is heuristic, and a wrong heuristic violates I1 (a long-offline clone rebasing pre-compaction events can resurrect a folded source whose .retired tombstone was GC'd).\n\nDecision needed: what stability model is acceptable? Options:\n1. Time-based configurable horizon (retain >= N days after the folding compaction commit): simplest, but PROBABILISTIC — cannot meet the 'provable' AC as written; would require the AC to be renegotiated to an operator-accepted risk window.\n2. Remote-anchored horizon: GC only tombstones whose compaction commit has been reachable from the sync remote's tickets ref for >= N days — stronger (any clone that pushes/pulls converges through the remote) but still unprovable for a clone that has never fetched.\n3. An explicit convergence/acknowledgment protocol (clones record observed-compaction watermarks in the store): the only path to a real proof; new event kind + doctrine change → needs an ADR, not a task.\n4. Keep permanent retention (b306 status quo) and close this as accepted-tradeoff if storage growth is not yet a real cost.\n\nRecommend the operator pick between (2) with a renegotiated AC, (3) as a designed epic, or (4). No code touched; ticket left open and unclaimed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787442664029028001,"uuid":"dfc17288-2378-4dfd-b1c1-1227885368a2"}